BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Painting III: Landscapes and Perspective
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T200000
UID:6a3554e2ba0ec7dc22619231@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this\nThird Part\nof a the Digital Painting Series\, learn 
 to create a digital landscape painting in Photoshop using the Wacom Tablet
 . Receive an introductory lesson on perspective and a walkthrough on how t
 o apply these skills to your digital painitng. Prior experience with a dra
 wing tablet is\nrequired\n\, as we will not being covering how to use the 
 equipment today.\nNOTE:\nIf you have never painted with a drawing tablet b
 efore\, please attend our First program in the series\,\nDigital Painting 
 I: Introduction & Pen Control\nor if you are looking an in depth look at t
 he broader aspects of Photoshop please look out for\nIntroduction to Photo
  Editing in Photoshop\nin our programs.\nFor more information about this p
 rogram please contact dihonline@tpl.ca.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Daniel G. Hill\, small Quiet Study Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3554e2ba0ec7dc22619231
