SUMMARY:Creating Interactive Fiction with Twine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T200000
UID:6a3301aa43b41b3d006f3309@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Choose your own adventure! In this hands-on workshop\, we'll b
 rowse examples of interactive fiction based on video games and touch on th
 e basics of storytelling. Then\, we'll create our own game using Twine\, a
 n open-source hypertext storytelling tool. Keyboarding and mouse skills ar
 e required. Located in the 2nd floor eLearning Lab.\nRegistration is requ
 ired for this class and begins July 6\, 2026 at 12:30 pm.\nNote: Your spot
  will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3301aa43b41b3d006f3309
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
