BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to A-Frame
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T200000
UID:6a05f8288e677a28001bf975@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A-Frame is a web framework for creating virtual reality (VR) 
 experiences with HyperText Markup Language (HTML)\, allowing developers 
 to create 3D and VR content using familiar HTML markup that works across d
 esktop or laptop computers\, mobile devices\, and VR headsets.  This bas
 ic introduction involves typing code to create simple objects and environm
 ents in the online code editor CodePen.\nFamiliarity with HTML is recommen
 ded but not essential.\nRegistration is required and begins at 12:30pm on 
 June 16\, 2026.\nNote: Your spot is guaranteed only during the first 5 min
 utes of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informa
 tion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pub
 lic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wi
 ll only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluati
 on. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direct
 ed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge 
 Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a05f8288e677a28001bf975
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
