UID:6a037161278f7c2f008cb573@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Goldhawk Park branch and its neighbourhood is home to a v
 ariety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore 
 the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize di
 fferent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importan
 ce.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRegistr
 ation is required. Please register online or contact the branch if you nee
 d assistance. When registering\, please include the total number of people
  who will be attending the program\, including both adults and children.\n
 The tour will start and end at the Goldhawk Park branch program room and 
 will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be u
 neven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordi
 ngly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, wa
 ter\, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the e
 vent of severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of an alte
 rnative date.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram 
 series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.
 ​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Goldhawk Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a037161278f7c2f008cb573
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
