BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Serger Sewing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T200000
UID:6a08946317731928001a3572@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of operating our serger\, the Juki MO-735! 
   In this class we will go over the basic operation and key functions of 
 a serger sewing machine. Threading the machine and safety will be discusse
 d.\nBetween three and five threads are routinely used to sew a seam\, tr
 im off the raw edges & finish the edges all at the same time with the Juk
 i MO-735 serger.  However\, this workshop focuses solely on learning the 
 4-thread overlock stitch.\nThis course is mandatory in order to book the s
 erger.\nChildren under 13 must be accompanied by an adult\nRegistration re
 quires a library card and begins June 15\, 2026 at 12:30 p.m.\nNote: Your
  spot is guaranteed only for the first 5 minutes of the program.\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a08946317731928001a3572
