DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an afternoon screening of "F1".\nF1 (2025)\
 nRunning time: 155 minutes\nDirector: Joseph Kosinski\nStarring: Brad Pitt
 \, Javier Bardem\, Damson Idris\, and Kerry Condon\nIn the 1990s\, Sonny H
 ayes was Formula 1's most promising driver until an accident on the track 
 nearly ended his career. Thirty years later\, the owner of a struggling Fo
 rmula 1 team convinces Sonny to return to racing and become the best in th
 e world. Driving alongside the team's hotshot rookie\, Sonny soon learns t
 hat the road to redemption is not something you can travel alone.\nThere i
 s a short\, informal discussion after the screening\, time permitting.\nRe
 gistration is not required. Please contact the Browsery Department at 416-
 395-5672 for more information.\nNext dates:\nJuly 22 (Wednesday\,\nat 6 PM
 \n) -\nSpecial Movie Night\n: Black Bag\nAugust 19 (Wednesday\, at 2 PM) :
  The Fantastic 4:\nFirst Steps
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a29b06d43b41b3d006d5d3a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rulers in Space: Measuring Distances in the Universe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T153000
UID:69dfb6ab129f12743838ac1b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered how we are able to measure distances in
  the Solar System\, in our Galaxy\, and beyond? Grab your cosmic ruler and
  embark on an exploration of the methods used to infer distances in the Un
 iverse — the result of centuries of innovative thinking by countless gen
 erations of astronomers. Join Dr. Gustavo Medina Toledo\, a postdoctoral r
 esearcher from Dunlap Institute for Astronomy & Astrophysics at the Univer
 sity of Toronto\, for a fascinating talk on this topic.\nRegistration is e
 ncouraged\n. Drop-ins are welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dfb6ab129f12743838ac1b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
