UID:6a16052e8e677a28001e9e04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to create your own comic\, manga\, or ani
 me-inspired story? In this interactive workshop\, teens will learn the bas
 ics of comic creation through hands-on activities\, creative storytelling\
 , and guided drawing exercises.\nParticipants will explore comic and manga
  techniques including panels\, page layouts\, speech bubbles\, sound effec
 ts\, character design\, and visual storytelling. They’ll also learn how 
 to build engaging characters and create their own one-page comic or manga 
 scene.\nLed by a published comic writer\, this workshop includes live demo
 nstrations\, creative prompts\, and opportunities to ask questions about c
 omics\, manga\, anime storytelling\, and the creative industry. Perfect fo
 r aspiring artists\, writers\, anime/manga fans\, and anyone curious about
  creating their own stories in a fun\, supportive environment.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Amesbury Park\, Program Room
