BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Journaling for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T173000
UID:6a1608128e677a28001e9fe2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a chill creative space to relax\, make art\, and e
 xpress yourself? In this fun and low-pressure workshop\, teens will explor
 e art journaling through painting\, collage\, doodling\, creative letterin
 g\, and writing prompts — no artistic experience needed.\nParticipants w
 ill experiment with layered backgrounds\, magazine cutouts\, aesthetic jou
 rnal styles\, quotes\, stickers\, and mixed media techniques to create pag
 es that reflect their personality\, interests\, and mood. Whether your vib
 e is messy and expressive\, cozy and aesthetic\, bold and colourful\, or i
 nspired by fandoms\, music\, anime\, or pop culture\, this is your space t
 o create freely.\nThe session begins with a guided prompt and creative ins
 piration before teens work at their own pace in a supportive and welcoming
  environment. There’s no “right way” to journal — the focus is on 
 creativity\, self-expression\, and having fun rather than making something
  perfect.\nFacilitated by artist Anna Redish\, this workshop encourages cr
 eativity\, confidence\, and individuality while giving teens the opportuni
 ty to unwind\, get inspired\, and connect with other creative people.\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
  and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how t
 he library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at
 \nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2
 G8.
LOCATION:Amesbury Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1608128e677a28001e9fe2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
